@startuml uc-stock-transfer
title UC: Branch-to-Branch Stock Transfer
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #2563EB
  ActorBorderColor #0F172A
  ActorBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  ParticipantBorderColor #0F172A
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
  NoteBackgroundColor #FEF9C3
  NoteBorderColor #CA8A04
}

actor "Store Manager\n(sending branch)" as Sender
actor "Staff\n(receiving branch)" as Receiver
participant "This Branch's\nPOS System" as System

== Sending branch ==
Sender -> System : POST /transfer(destinationBranch, items[])
System -> System : create stock_transfers row (status: pending,\nfrom_branch_id = this branch)
System -> System : create stock_transfer_items lines
System -> System : append stock_movements\n(movement_type: transfer_out, -qty_delta)
System -> System : decrement products.quantity immediately
System -> System : write audit_log + sync_outbox entry
System --> Sender : transfer recorded (pending)

note over System
  Stock leaves this branch's ledger the moment
  the transfer is recorded, not when it's later
  received elsewhere — the goods have physically left.
end note

== Physical goods arrive ==

== Receiving branch ==
Receiver -> System : POST /transfer/:id/receive
System -> System : credit stock back\n(movement_type: transfer_in, +qty_delta)
System -> System : increment products.quantity
System -> System : status -> received;\nstamp received_by / received_at
System --> Receiver : transfer received

== Exceptions ==
alt no destination branch or no line items
  System --> Sender : 400 rejected
end
alt second receive attempt on same transfer
  System --> Receiver : 400 "Transfer already received"
end
note over Sender, Receiver
  Scope note: each Electron install is one branch's
  own local database. Automatic cross-branch routing
  (the other branch auto-seeing this transfer) needs
  the cloud sync API's multi-branch model — planned
  Phase 5, not yet built. Until then, receiving staff
  record the receipt themselves once goods arrive.
end note
@enduml
